// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6451 Add macOS encoded payload piped to shell rule
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6451
// Pull request author: yana-ivanov
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Encoded Payload Piped To Shell - macOS
// Sigma ID: b9a60caf-969e-4033-9513-2f097adee039
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Yana Ivanov
// Date: 2026-10-10 | Modified: 2026-11-15
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, command-and-control, T1059.004, T1105, T1027
// Description: Detects a command line that downloads content with curl, decodes it with base64, gunzip or xxd,
//   and pipes the result into a shell interpreter, in that order. This chain is used by macOS
//   ClickFix campaigns and by the MacSync and AMOS infostealer infection chains. The rule matches
//   only where the whole pipeline appears in a single command line. On macOS that happens when a
//   shell is invoked with -c, or when the chain is run through osascript 'do shell script'. When a
//   user pastes a pipeline directly into an interactive Terminal, each stage is executed as its own
//   process and no single process_creation event contains the chain, so that case is not covered by
//   this rule. The decode step is what separates this from legitimate installer one-liners, which
//   fetch and execute without decoding.
// False positives:
//   - Installation and bootstrap scripts that fetch a compressed archive and pipe it through a shell
//   - Developer and CI tooling that unpacks a downloaded archive inline
//   - Provisioning and automation scripts invoked through 'sh -c'
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/08/18/hunting-macsync-stealer-infrastructure-through-behavioral-pivots/
//   - https://securelist.com/macsync-new-version/121383/
//   - https://hunt.io/blog/macos-clickfix-applescript-terminal-phishing
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/atomic-macos-amos-stealer-activity
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/73736c4670a8739b60867f7d3d9727fcfbacc976/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_susp_encoded_payload_piped_to_shell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine matches regex "curl.*\\|.*\\b(base64\\s+(-d|-D|--decode)|gunzip|gzip\\s+-d|xxd\\s+-r)\\b.*\\|\\s*(\\S*/)?(ba|z)?sh\\b" and (((FolderPath endswith "/sh" or FolderPath endswith "/bash" or FolderPath endswith "/zsh") and ProcessCommandLine contains " -c ") or (FolderPath endswith "/osascript" and ProcessCommandLine contains "do shell script"))
